index 8bc22d4..4330667 100644
--- a/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
+++ b/docs/1.guide/1.basics/6.error.md
@@ -89,6 +89,50 @@ app.get("/error", (event) => {
 > [!TIP]
 > For enhanced security, H3 hides certain fields of unhandled errors (`data`, `body`, `stack` and `message`) in JSON response.
 
+## Problem Details (RFC 9457)
+
+Set `problemDetails: true` in the app config to render errors generated by H3 as [RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457.html) problem details, with `Content-Type: application/problem+json`. It is disabled by default.
+
+```js
+const app = new H3({ problemDetails: true });
+
+app.get("/orders/:id", () => {
+  throw new HTTPError({
+    status: 403,
+    statusText: "Forbidden",
+    message: "No permission",
+    type: "https://example.com/errors/no-permission",
+    instance: "/orders/42",
+  });
+});
+```
+
+This responds with `403` and the following body:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "https://example.com/errors/no-permission",
+  "title": "Forbidden",
+  "status": 403,
+  "detail": "No permission",
+  "instance": "/orders/42"
+}
+```
+
+The members map from the default JSON format as follows:
+
+- `status` ← `status`
+- `title` ← `statusText` (omitted when not set)
+- `detail` ← `message`
+- `type` ← `type`, or `about:blank` when not set
+- `instance` ← `instance` (omitted when not set)
+- `data` and `body` are added as extension members.
+
+> [!IMPORTANT]
+> Clients that read `message` or `statusText` from the default format must read `detail` and `title` instead. `type` and `instance` are not validated as URIs.
+
+Unhandled errors keep the same masking: `detail` is `"HTTPError"`, and `data` and `body` are omitted. With `debug: true`, a `stack` extension member is included. The option applies to the app that receives the request, so sub-apps use their own config.
+
 ## Catching Errors
 
 Using global [`onError`](/guide/api/h3#global-hooks) hook:
